While waiting, I re-checked the shadow tile logic and found a real bug. A tile is redrawn only through its casters, so when a caster leaves a tile, the atlas texels it covered keep their old depth values and create phantom occluders. A tile with no casters also never gets cleared. The fix is to treat the atlas as the unit of redraw: if any tile in an atlas changes, clear that atlas's color once and redraw all its granted tiles. Making that change now.
